        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pigments provide primary color and opacity (hiding power) by absorbing or scattering incident light, and have high refractive indices (e.g., rutile TiO2 has a refractive index of 2.73). Extenders (or fillers) are platy or ground minerals with low refractive indices (around 1.5 to 1.6) that contribute minimal color or hiding power, but are utilized to control gloss, build dry film thickness, improve mechanical properties, prevent pigment crowding, and optimize formulation costs."
